// Rule: nothing runs before main, so no package function may be named
// init, a name that says it runs first: it is refused in every
// package, called or not. Fix: give it another name and call it where
// it is needed, or let a package variable's initializer do the work,
// which runs once on the variable's first use.

package p

func init() { // ERROR "a package function cannot be named init: nothing runs before main"
}
